+        <h3>&ldquo;Direct only&rdquo; tells your contacts when you come online.</h3>
+        <p>From 0.2 you can use Night Drop with no relay at all. Then nothing about your messages
+           ever touches a server &mdash; but messages to you wait on your contacts' phones and are
+           sent the moment your app is online, so each contact can tell, roughly, when you come
+           online. With a relay, messages wait there instead. Opening the app does not announce
+           anything by itself.</p>
+        <p>It also means two people on direct only must be online at the same time for a message to
+           arrive. It waits on the sender's phone until then, with no 24-hour limit.</p>
