+        <h3>Your QR code lets one person knock, for one day.</h3>
+        <p>So that pairing needs no server, your invite carries a key that lets whoever has it reach
+           your phone even once it only accepts your contacts. That gets their chat request to you,
+           and nothing else: you still decide whether to accept it, and until you do they learn
+           nothing about you. The key stops working once one request has used it, or after a day. So
+           a photo of your QR code posted online lets at most one stranger send you a request you can
+           decline.</p>
